  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical uncertainty is whether each modality individually carries sufficient signal for the classification task, and what performance floor we should expect. Config_005 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is the simplest, cleanest baseline: it uses a well-established RNA encoder (scgpt), the simplest profile setting, and no image processing or fusion. Establishing the RNA-only performance first provides an essential reference point against which all subsequent image-only and multimodal results can be meaningfully compared. Without this baseline, a multimodal result would be uninterpretable—we could not tell whether fusion is adding value or merely matching a strong single-modality model. This experiment is also computationally lightweight, conserving budget for the multimodal experiments that follow."
}

